  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual metaphor in the meme",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'the blacker the berry the sweeter the juice' as the core object of the meme's semiotic projection. This phrase, historically a racial stereotype, is used here to imply a value judgment about women's desirability based on skin tone, and the user is invited to identify with or interpret this metaphor in the context of the 'chicks be like' framing. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you' in the text, but the meme format inherently projects the viewer as the one making the humorous or ironic observation, thus projecting the user onto the textual metaphor as the interpretive subject.",
